This supplement makes paths and service defaults portable, removes identifying
metadata and historical outputs, extracts shared model/diagnostic code, and
removes unrelated experiment frameworks. Evaluation entry points and presets
are restricted to the final manuscript. The MathlibQR entry point uses the
shared retrieval backend. PAPER_SETTINGS.md records settings that differ from
historical working configurations. Core retrieval and verification code and
paper prompt text are retained. Third-party attribution appears in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and the benchmark license files.
